# Performance And SEO

## Performance

- Prefer Server Components and server data fetching when interactivity is not needed.
- Use dynamic imports only for heavy or rarely used client components, not as a default.
- Avoid unnecessary client boundaries, effects, and global state.
- Keep repeated expensive computations in helpers, constants, memoized values, or server code based on where they run.
- Optimize lists by extracting stable item components when rendering becomes expensive or complex.

## Rendering

- Choose SSG, SSR, ISR, or client rendering intentionally.
- Set `cache`, `next.revalidate`, or `dynamic` behavior explicitly when data freshness matters.
- Do not fetch the same data in multiple layers of the same route unless required.

## SEO

- Use the Next.js Metadata API for indexable pages.
- Keep page titles, descriptions, headings, and Open Graph fields aligned with the actual page content.
- Use semantic headings and avoid skipping heading levels in public content pages.
